  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "AND, OR, and XOR evaluate direct arguments before references/arrays and skip direct non-boolean text unless no logical is found",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527.20088, AND, OR, and XOR inspect every argument in two passes: all direct arguments first, then references and array constants. Direct errors therefore precede errors inside arrays or references (AND({TRUE,#N/A},#DIV/0!) is #DIV/0!). Direct text \"TRUE\" and \"FALSE\" parse as logicals, whereas other direct text (\"x\", \"1\", \"0\", \"\") is skipped when at least one logical is read (AND(TRUE,\"x\") is TRUE, OR(FALSE,\"x\") is FALSE) and gives #VALUE! when none is read (AND(\"x\"), OR(\"x\",\"y\")). Inside arrays and references, all text (including \"TRUE\") is skipped; omitted direct arguments read as FALSE in AND/OR and are ignored or FALSE in XOR (XOR(TRUE,) is TRUE).",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across all 115 Excel 16.0.20527.20088 readings in dc_fwpz (logical_functions rows 3-85) and matched across 1,210/1,210 AND, 1,212/1,212 OR, and 1,212/1,212 XOR full-bank rows.",
